<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eric II, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1425–<a href="/years/1474">1474</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eric II (c. 1425–1474) was a Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a> and, after the death of his relative King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-of-pomerania">Eric of Pomerania</a> in 1459, also the eastern lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slupsk">Stolp</a>. He fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> over the succession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a>, a dispute settled by the Treaty of Prenzlau in 1472. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-x">Bogislaw X</a> reunited all the Pomeranian lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eric-ii-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Eric II, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C Schleyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pommersches_Landesmuseum-Herzog_Erich_II._von_Pommern-Wolgast-WUS08656.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
